# Test: ze config validate REFUSES a dh-group outside the range the data model
# assigns. RFC 7296 Section 3.3.2 gives Transform Type 4 the range this leaf
# encodes as `range "1..31"`, and the YANG schema is what enforces it.
#
# Deliberately NOT asserted here: that a dh-group INSIDE the range but absent
# from the crypto registry (5, for example) is refused. DHGroupImplemented closes
# that -- it was the defect this work package fixed -- but it runs in
# parseIKEProposal, which `ze config validate` does not invoke, exactly as it does
# not invoke the encryption and hash gates beside it. Unit proof:
# TestIKESuitePolicyRejectsAnUnhonourableSuite row 3
# (internal/component/ike/ipsec/rfc7296_test.go).
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65533
				remote 65533
			}
		}
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		ike-group IKE-BAD-DH {
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256gcm
				hash sha256
				dh-group 32
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=configuration invalid
expect=stdout:contains=dh-group
